   "is_root": true,
   "etymology": "First attested in 1497. The short nasal vowel in the 3rd sg. blê \"to buy\" and the long nasal in the 1st-3rd sg. blẽ \"id.\" point to a Common Albanian *blên, inherited from Proto-Albanian *blêna/i-, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *blena/e-, from either Proto-Indo-European *h₃bʰloi̯éi̯e/o- (“to buy”) or Proto-Indo-European *bʰl̥nh₂énti (“to buy”). A reasonable formal and semantic match is found in Ancient Greek ὄφελος (óphelos, “advantage, help”).",
   "etymology_class": "inherited",
   "source_lang": null,
